IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `sta-strata`

-- Strata Titles Act 1985 (WA), ss 46, 47, 100, 102, 110, 120, 123, 126, 156-164, 197, 210 and regs 58, 78-81, 86, 162 -- worked cases.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Nothing here has been checked
-- against a decided case. The regulations' numbers are from the deposited Strata Titles (General) Regulations 2019.
--
-- Fixtures are generated from a table of which flags are set (scratchpad gen_wa_strata-titles-act-1985_baseline.py). Expected results were written by
-- hand from the text.

-- Facts from the WA lives (workbench scenarios au/wa/cradle-to-grave-{chloe,jake,daniel}). The scenarios give no
-- unit entitlements, budgets, lot counts or mortgages for the three apartments, so every such figure used with them is
-- the encoder's, chosen for arithmetic:
--   chloe c094 (2070): a Mandurah apartment, bought resale with Liam as co-owners, no mortgage; 24 lots, unit
--     entitlement 42 of 1 000; administrative budget $96 000, reserve budget $30 000.
--   daniel d037 (2028): an East Perth apartment, $1 600 000, with Priya as joint tenants, mortgaged; 200 lots, unit
--     entitlement 85 of 10 000; administrative budget $2 400 000, reserve budget $800 000.
--   jake k076 (2045, contract 2042): a one-bedroom apartment bought off the plan from the developer for $390 000 with a
--     Keystart loan (mortgaged), sole owner; 60 lots, estimated unit entitlement 30 of 2 000, registered as 32 of 2 000;
--     administrative budget $180 000, reserve budget $60 000; a 5% deposit of $19 500 held on trust.

§ `fixtures`

`a quiet-hours by-law` MEANS `What the by-law does` WITH
    `is beyond any power to make it` IS FALSE
    `is inconsistent with the Act or another written law` IS FALSE
    `is inconsistent with a restricted use condition` IS FALSE
    `denies or limits a member's vote` IS FALSE
    `restricts selling, leasing, mortgaging or passing on a lot` IS FALSE
    `discharges or modifies an easement or restrictive covenant` IS FALSE
    `restricts an assistance animal of a person with a disability` IS FALSE
    `is unfairly prejudicial, discriminatory, oppressive or unreasonable, as the Tribunal finds` IS FALSE

`a ban on dogs that covers assistance dogs` MEANS `What the by-law does` WITH
    `is beyond any power to make it` IS FALSE
    `is inconsistent with the Act or another written law` IS FALSE
    `is inconsistent with a restricted use condition` IS FALSE
    `denies or limits a member's vote` IS FALSE
    `restricts selling, leasing, mortgaging or passing on a lot` IS FALSE
    `discharges or modifies an easement or restrictive covenant` IS FALSE
    `restricts an assistance animal of a person with a disability` IS TRUE
    `is unfairly prejudicial, discriminatory, oppressive or unreasonable, as the Tribunal finds` IS FALSE

`a ban on leasing lots` MEANS `What the by-law does` WITH
    `is beyond any power to make it` IS FALSE
    `is inconsistent with the Act or another written law` IS FALSE
    `is inconsistent with a restricted use condition` IS FALSE
    `denies or limits a member's vote` IS FALSE
    `restricts selling, leasing, mortgaging or passing on a lot` IS TRUE
    `discharges or modifies an easement or restrictive covenant` IS FALSE
    `restricts an assistance animal of a person with a disability` IS FALSE
    `is unfairly prejudicial, discriminatory, oppressive or unreasonable, as the Tribunal finds` IS FALSE

